Straight from the rough list of queue/audits/2026-09-17-icon-width-row-nothing-picked.json: 'The icon previews strip still vanishes the moment you pick nothing, for the same reason the Width row used to go wrong: it only knows which icon it is showing from what is picked. It was left alone here so this change stayed to one row.'

The code says the same. Sources/Photonz/EditorState+IconPreviews.swift:

    var iconPreviewFrameID: UUID? {
        guard iconPreviewsEnabled, let document, let id = selectedLayerID else { return nil }
        return document.iconFrameID(containing: id)
    }

No selectedLayerID, no frame, and iconPreviewTiles returns [] so the strip draws nothing.

The answer already exists one file away: with-nothing-picked-the-pen-s-width-row-still-sa (done, commit 2c1a4bc4) taught the Width row to fall back to the icon frame UNDER THE POINTER when nothing is picked. Reuse that, do not invent a second rule. That task's audit also records the one flaw worth not repeating: sweep the pointer out of the frame onto bare canvas and the row can read stale, so decide deliberately what the previews show when the pointer is over neither.

Drawing surface: Sources/Photonz/IconPreviewsStrip.swift, Sources/Photonz/IconPreviewsOverlay.swift.
